      "id": "psychology-06",
      "beat": "discovery",
      "narration": "Researchers call one version of this distinction self-concordance: how well a goal fits your interests and values. Sheldon and Elliot's research linked more self-concordant goals with sustained effort and attainment. That is evidence about motivation, not a guarantee that meaningful goals become easy.",
