    {
      "id": "psychology-10",
      "beat": "conflict",
      "narration": "In his imagination, writing a story means dragging an entire mountain into his apartment. Plot. Style. Dialogue. Being good enough. His first step isn't a step. It's a final exam he has invented before writing a single sentence.",
